/target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.lock

# Captured frames: the bulk corpora are not committed, curated evidence is.
#
# fixtures/frames/ holds the 120-frame decode-benchmark corpus (~32 MB) of an idle
# desktop. It is reproducible by re-running the capture spike and is excluded.
#
# fixtures/frames/absrange/ is different and is deliberately KEPT: fifteen curated
# frames that are the visual proof for the absolute-coordinate finding (§3.4), showing
# where the cursor actually lands at full scale and past the wrap. Small, and not
# reproducible if the target's screen changes. Do not "tidy" these away.
/fixtures/frames/*.jpg
/fixtures/frames/*.jpeg
/fixtures/frames/*.raw
/fixtures/frames/*.yuv
/fixtures/traffic/*.pcap
/fixtures/traffic/*.bin

# Read-only upstream reference checkout, not part of this project.
/reference/

# sysfs fixture trees: build output, not source.
#
# The source is fixtures/sysfs/usb2-desk.sysfs — the 2026-09-10 recording of this desk,
# serialised to one line-oriented file — plus fixtures/sysfs/synthesize.py, which expands it
# and reconstructs the other trees from it. Expanded, they are ~1300 one-line files.
# `cargo test` materialises them on demand (src/discovery/testing.rs), or run
# `python3 fixtures/sysfs/synthesize.py` by hand. Every subdirectory is ignored, so a new
# tree needs no entry here; only the top-level files are tracked.
/fixtures/sysfs/*/
/fixtures/sysfs/.synthesize.lock
__pycache__/
